title The eighth door walked -- the platform cancels a real drag mid-flight, and the cancellation crosses the ring in order
prompt Keaton's kg on the movement; the parked cancellation road turned out to exist, and the crux took it.
think The honest cancellation is a real interruption: another application taking the screen mid-drag. Two clocks make it -- a background fuse launching Settings, and a slow swipe under it -- and the handler now schedules the close exactly as a lift does, while the drain accepts a drag's two honest endings: the finger lifts, or the platform cancels, moves and nothing else between.
think The race cost three attempts and taught the instrument truth: this bench's tool round-trip eats seconds, so short fuses die before the finger lands, and the touch_path action delivered nothing where the swipe action delivers -- the proven instrument with a twelve-second fuse under a twenty-second swipe finally crossed. On metal: down at (95,130), twelve moves, CANCELLED -- kind eight admitted by the platform's own dispatch, drained in order, GREEN with the cancelled terminal named.
obs The up terminal reran GREEN on the same build -- down, twenty-seven moves, up -- so both endings of a drag stand proven on one binary, and the domain event's eight doors have all now been walked by the platform itself: keys and mouse on macOS, four touch phases on iOS. The cancelled location arrives in raw coordinates after the window resigns, which is honest platform data and recorded as such.
loom probe=ios_touch_ring cancel_moves=12 cancel_at=(526,1214) up_leg_moves=27 attempts=4 fuse=12s
